patrone-desktop (0.1.6) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Automatic security updates work again: unattended-upgrades allows
    Ubuntu's origins by name (52patrone-unattended-upgrades), since its own
    file names them by the system's ID, now "Patrone".
  * Software & Updates knows the archive: python-apt's templates for
    "patrone" are Ubuntu's.
  * `apt upgrade` no longer advertises Ubuntu Pro (its apt hook is moved
    aside), and the session leaves out Ubuntu's web search (client=ubuntu)
    and App Center's search. From a search of the installed system for
    Ubuntu's name (the user, 2026-10-27).
  * No "Ubuntu Pro is available" at login: conflicts with update-notifier,
    whose place in Ubuntu's desktop (ubuntu-desktop-minimal needs one) it
    takes, so removing it doesn't bring in GNOME's Package Updater, and with
    ubuntu-advantage-desktop-daemon, Ubuntu Pro's desktop service.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 19:30:00 -0500

patrone-desktop (0.1.5) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Patrone's taskbar is one of the session's own extensions: Ubuntu's
    session mode for GNOME Shell (ubuntu.json, moved aside) with the
    taskbar added, remade whenever gnome-shell-common updates it. GNOME
    turns off the other extensions after a crash early in a session, and
    with the taskbar off its own top bar came back; session extensions
    always load.

 -- William Daugherty <31995458+billsecond@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:05:00 -0500

